WEBVTT

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.490
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.080
Good morning, Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:03.430
"Episode 6: Beyond a Pale Light"

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.360
Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.430
Don't worry. They'll find
out soon you're innocent.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.680
Yeah. Thanks.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.770
Make sure you eat breakfast.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:09.680
Sure.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.270
Okay, see you later!

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.580
I have to get into Geotech
if I want to prove her innocence.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.090
Ayumi-<i>san</i>'s innocence...

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.170
What's this?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.800
What does it look like?

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.580
The Grand Canyon,
filled with the dreams of men?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.640
Your penalty for cutting class yesterday.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.060
This is going too far.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.980
You need to finish it all,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.530
or you'll be spending that summer
you were looking forward to in a classroom.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.190
Boss, summer's waiting!

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.110
Let's finish this up and
go to the beach! The beach!

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.370
The beach?

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.290
That's right! The bikinis are calling me!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.950
Yuki-<i>kun</i>, leave him alone.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:13.250
There's nothing in
Arima-<i>kun</i>'s head but dirty fantasies.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.540
What's your problem?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.820
There's no swimming allowed at the beach
due to the Geotech construction project.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.180
Okay, class is starting!

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.220
Arima, get your butt in gear,
or you'll miss the whole summer.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.970
Crap...

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:36.020
Takuya Arima-<i>kun</i>, please come
to the broadcasting room immediately.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.400
--Takuya Arima-<i>kun</i>, please come
to the broadcasting room immediately.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.400
--This voice...

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.570
Again?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.200
You're a lucky guy, boss.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.200
You heard the lady.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.470
Yuki will do it for me.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.520
I'm not even in your grade!
How am I supposed to know the answers?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.490
It'll be good practice.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.520
I knew it was you.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.510
You did, huh?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:09.810
This is one of those times when
it's rough being a popular newscaster.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.440
What happened to Toyotomi?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.850
You took care of him, right?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.390
Of course.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:21.180
Everything's been arranged
for him to leave Geotech.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:25.240
He'll probably never 
bother Chief Arima again.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.240
How'd you pull that off?
You don't work for Geotech.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.500
I'm a journalist.
So I've got lots of connections.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:39.290
He's been given a good offer to work
for another firm. No one will suspect a thing.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.790
So he just gets another job, then?

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.010
And a few days later, he gets fired.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.560
He won't be going to jail,
but that's punishment enough, right?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.930
Don't worry.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.860
I've got a plan to save your mom.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.280
You're going to break into
Geotech and find proof, right?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.340
How did you know?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.450
No reason. I'm just smart, is all.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.910
Then it'll be good to have you around.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.540
You'll make the perfect partner for me.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.600
Partner?

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.460
Sheesh...

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.800
What am I even doing here?

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.300
You shouldn't let a pretty girl
like me be alone at night.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.060
You're seriously planning on breaking in?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.520
Of course.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.850
That's what the blue card is for, right?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.270
You managed to give her the fake one, right?

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.190
Yeah.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.360
I'd already done it once before.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.350
Once before?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:42.940
What does that mean?

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.440
Nothing.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.040
Security looks tougher than I thought.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.780
How would you get in, then?

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.000
It feels like I'm being tested.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.840
It feels that way because I'm testing you.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.920
Let me see...

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.180
What about that dome?

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.260
Which one?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.970
Look. That concealed dome.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.450
The con-dome.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.270
Hey, stop screwing around.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.560
Right, right.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.020
Well, the safe answer
would be the rear entrance.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.650
Not a bad answer at all.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.740
It doesn't look heavily guarded.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.170
Okay, see you inside Geotech.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.990
You're not breaking in?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:38.750
I'm with the media.
I get to go in through the front door.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.370
Unlike you.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.540
Hey, that's not fair.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.380
I'll unlock the back door
for you when I'm inside.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.670
Don't leave me waiting, Romeo!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.120
Sheesh...

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.100
What a self-centered Juliet.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.290
Not yet, huh?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:13.240
Mother, you know how I feel.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.470
Please, not another word.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.040
Hello.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.540
What can I do for you?

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.330
I'm here for an interview.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.000
I'll open the gate for you.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:31.510
"Geotechnics"

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.630
Working late tonight, huh?

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.510
Yeah. Tell your bosses
that this is getting ridiculous.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.700
Is she still not here?

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.480
Shit, that's not good...

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.120
Glad you made it, Romeo.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.330
You're late, Juliet.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.420
Were you putting on
your sexiest panties for me?

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.370
Quit whining. You were fine, right?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.250
Sheesh.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.180
This is Sector A outdoor patrol.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.330
Sector A outdoor patrol, reporting in.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.980
This is the guard house.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.770
Anything odd on the security cameras?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.860
Huh? Um... nope.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.310
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:33.990
Roger.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.070
I'll keep patrolling the outside.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.530
Sounds good!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.250
Roger...

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.000
It's quiet here at night.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:54.510
Everybody's in a meeting deciding
what to do about your mother.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:58.300
You can really prove her innocence?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.060
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.070
I can, as long as I can 
get through this door.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.000
It's time, huh?

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:21.660
However, I'm afraid we're not quite done.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:24.080
Don't waste my time, then!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:29.290
We need this light here
to turn blue before we can open it.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.590
Somebody needs to be
in the control room to unlock it.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.590
And that's why you made me your partner?

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.140
You are smart!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.180
I'll go to the control room.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.860
You open the door.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.100
Do it quick this time.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.600
Sure.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:53.480
Sometimes... I'm a woman too.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.590
M-Mother!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.450
No! You mustn't! No!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.490
I don't care! We're not really related!

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.500
Is she still not done?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.500
Okay.

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.040
Sector D-12.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.780
This is the heart of Geotech.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:26.370
Geotechnics' real goal
is to excavate these rocks.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.380
What do they want with some rocks?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.890
You'll realize how amazing
they are in a minute.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:37.610
Dr. Kodai Arima was interested in them too.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:39.830
My dad?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.210
What is this?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.230
A new type of luminescent ore.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:11:03.480
Dr. Arima gave it this name
after its unique properties: psychite.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.330
Psychite?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.440
It's so wonderful...

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.310
The blue light of life...

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.320
What is this stone?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.540
Why did my dad care about it?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.080
Psychite was first excavated
beneath Mt. Sankaku.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.170
Immediately after it was,
its strange properties were recognized.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.840
What properties?

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.470
It's a miraculous stone that

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.360
reacts to the human mind
and creates vast amounts of energy.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:47.590
Some people thought it
may be a type of living ore.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.340
Did those people just
watch too many sci-fi movies?

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:56.570
It's certainly a mystery why a strange rock
like that would be beneath Sakaimachi.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:00.360
But it's got a weak point.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:01.510
A weak point?

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.990
You saw the ones in the entrance, right?

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.700
Its molecular bonds are unstable.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:10.250
Just making contact
with air changes its properties.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.850
That's why there was a need
to crystallize it, like you see here.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.660
Of course, it seems
like this is the only sample.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.470
Is that "crystallization"...

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:23.590
Yes.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:28.640
That's what your mother,
Chief Arima, was researching here.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.840
At Dr. Kodai Arima's request.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.860
My dad asked her to do it?

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:42.440
Toyotomi made Chief Arima
take the fall for the data theft.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:47.070
Next, he'll try to come get the psychite.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.330
And?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.830
This'll do it.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.960
Use this to break the tank open.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.500
You're going to make it so everyone
knows what he's done, right?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.000
You want me to do it?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.550
I've got a recording to do tomorrow.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.100
I don't want to get hurt.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.590
Fine.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.610
This thing is pretty thick.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.500
Just do it!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.430
This is for Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.500
Emergency!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.920
Everyone, come in!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.840
Here, now...

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.100
You done?

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.070
Toyotomi...

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.490
That was amazing.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:06.240
Perfect, right?

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:09.620
Between the fingerprints
on the glass and the rear doorknob,

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.080
he'll take all the blame.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.790
Thanks, slacker son.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:18.990
You were working together?

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.590
The guards will be here soon.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.750
Let's go.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:23.580
Yeah.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.470
Have fun talking to the cops.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:49.240
However, I'm afraid we're not quite done.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:52.160
You need to unlock the door
from the control room, right?

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.330
Huh? You knew?

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.450
You didn't hear that from your mom, did you?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.580
You see it in video games all the time.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.170
Do you?

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.880
Well, whatever.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.920
I'll be heading to the control room.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:06.960
You wait here.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.610
Hurry.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:12.510
Sure thing.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.060
Shit... Now what do I do?

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:21.740
I know what happens next,
but I don't know how to stop it.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:25.980
Sometimes... I'm a woman too.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.320
M-Mother!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.950
No! You mustn't! No!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.740
--I don't care! We're not really related!
--Is it finally happening?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.230
Psychite...

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.230
Emergency!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.050
Everyone, come in!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.490
Here, now...

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.000
You done?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.300
Damn, I knew it was coming and it still hurt.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.550
That was amazing.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:31.970
Perfect, right?

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.690
Yeah. Nice work.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:39.180
The plan to make me into
the thief was a good idea, too.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:39.980
What?

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:44.060
That's going beyond "smart."

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:46.980
But why make me the thief?

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.570
Chief Arima is in a very bad position.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.150
The accidents. The criticism.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.210
The suspicion of data theft.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:01.470
To save herself, she came up with a plan.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:06.290
She would have her stepson
steal the research materials.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.460
Who'd believe that bullshit?

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:11.760
There's no need for the truth,

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.590
and what the police want to know,
to be the same thing.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:20.490
As long as they find your fingerprints,
the evidence makes you the culprit.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.860
I knew Toyotomi was a scumbag.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:25.910
But you too, Kaori-<i>san</i>?

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.400
Why?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.020
I'm a journalist.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.650
My job is to find hidden truths.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.950
He and I want very different things.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.120
Yeah, that's a bunch of bullshit.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.120
You're an industrial spy.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.660
Don't be rude.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:45.620
It's true, isn't it?

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:51.090
You blackmail companies for money,
and then report on them in your program.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:54.090
And you call that journalism, huh?

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.510
Who was your employer this time?

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.390
Someone from a school...

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:03.140
We're wasting time. Let's finish up here.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.890
Yeah, that's true.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.350
You've only yourself
to blame for this, slacker son.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.440
Sorry. You're going to jail, not me.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.070
It's already over, kid.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.740
Nobody will believe a word you said.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.030
Well...

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.320
I don't know about that.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.490
Wait, is this turning you on?

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.410
Oh my!

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:28.760
I wanted to make sure
everyone heard what you said.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.140
So I borrowed this.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:36.080
Every guard in this facility is a witness.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.720
We heard it all!

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.900
Game over.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.230
In the end, the good guys always win!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.820
Don't push me!

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.070
This woman did it all!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.380
Call my lawyer! Now!

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:02.990
"Geotechnics"

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.160
Thank you so much...

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.460
Thanks to you, I can continue my research.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.670
Dad asked you to do that research, huh?

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:15.880
That's right.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:20.340
He asked me to find a way
to crystallize psychite.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.640
The light disappeared.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.430
Because it touched the air.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:28.240
We haven't succeeded
in perfect crystallization yet.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:34.650
I never understood why Kodai-<i>san</i>
was so obsessed with this stone.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:39.630
But the journal he would
always be writing in his study...

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:48.360
I found it when I was cleaning the room.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.790
What did it say?

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:56.730
He still loves your real mother.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:00.400
That's what his research 
into psychite was for.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.720
What is this?

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:11.020
It looks like it's time
for you to leave this world.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.340
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:18.220
Kodai-<i>san</i>'s journal talked
about the parallel worlds, too.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:22.720
I don't know what world you're from, but...

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.830
Return to your path.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.340
The one you belong to.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.400
Thank you, Takuya-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:54.560
Dad?

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:57.770
It's impossible to resist causality.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.760
This is the correction of chaos.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.900
The correction of chaos?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:11.450
It seems that you weren't
meant to be there after all.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.330
You will be sent back to the start.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.070
What are you saying?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:20.630
You will experience the 
same events over again.

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:24.930
But don't forget that
they'll be slightly different.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:28.320
How do you know this?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.480
Because I rest against the Tree of Vrinda,

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:39.690
which rules over all events,
past, present, and future.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:43.010
I knew it. You're still alive.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:46.110
Takuya, remember this.

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:48.940
Causality rules everything in this world.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:53.410
To discover its secrets 
is to explore history.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.210
What does that mean?

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:56.920
Hey, answer me!

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:00.590
Dad! Dad!

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:41.650
"Episode 7: The Cause of the Curse"

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:39.290
Episode 7: "The Cause of the Curse."
